@nvcnvn Could you help review this serving-benchmark streaming-error fix or route it to the appropriate maintainer? The updated head is `36264a75b1`, which contains the required `MIN_BASE_SHA` (`8854857a99`), and the PR still changes only the original two files.

When a Chat Completions SSE response carries an error (including after partial content), the benchmark currently can count the request as successful. The fix rejects these error responses rather than allowing them to inflate success metrics. The two error-handling regressions fail against the pre-fix implementation; all 13 focused streaming tests pass on the updated branch in a fresh environment on my local 5090 machine. The repository-version isort, selected Ruff rules, formatting, codespell, CI test-registration validation, and `git diff --check` also pass.

Could an authorized maintainer enable `run-ci` and review this change? The previously reported green lint applies to the earlier head; the workflows for this push are new. Thank you.

